  "panelText": "Summarize this page in 3 sentences\n存成技能\nHayao Miyazaki - Wikipedia\n\nHayao Miyazaki is a Japanese animator, filmmaker, and manga artist, born January 5, 1941 in Tokyo City, who co-founded Studio Ghibli in 1985 and serves as its honorary chairman. Beginning at Toei Animation in 1963, he worked his way through studios like A-Pro, Zuiyō Eizō/Nippon Animation, and Tokyo Movie Shinsha, directing early works including Lupin the Third Part I (with Isao Takahata), Future Boy Conan, and his feature debut The Castle of Cagliostro (1979). Through Studio Ghibli he created internationally acclaimed films such as Nausicaä of the Valley of the Wind (1984), My Neighbor Totoro, Princess Mononoke, and Spirited Away, earning recognition as one of the greatest storytellers in the history of animation.",
